# TwinCAT MCP Format (Python Formatter)

Use when the user asks to format Structured Text, "Format code",
or `/twincat3-cmd-format`. This is the **default** format path.
Detailed workflow: skill `twincat3-format`.

For STweep via XAE COM (explicit request only): rule `twincat3-mcp-stweep` /
skill `twincat3-stweep-format` / command `/twincat3-cmd-stweep-format`.

## Tools (file-based, no COM/XAE session required)

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `twincat_format` | Format files/folders/project — ST code + XML structure |
| `twincat_format_progress` | Poll running format job (large projects) |
| `twincat_format_validate` | Validate-only (XML structure, GUIDs, naming) — no format |
| `twincat_format_config` | Show active config (defaults + project overrides) |

No `twincat_open` needed. Operates directly on `.TcPOU` / `.TcDUT` / `.TcGVL` / `.TcIO` files via `twincat_core.xml` surgical patching and `twincat_core.syntax` token/CST engine.

## Core parameters (`twincat_format`)

| Parameter | Default | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|---------|
| `path` | required | File, folder, or project root |
| `recursive` | `true` | Recurse into subfolders |
| `dry_run` | `false` | Preview changes without writing |
| `validate` | `true` | Run XML validation after format |
| `format_xml` | `true` | Format XML structure (indent, attribute order) |
| `sort_elements` | `false` | Alphabetically sort Methods/Actions/Properties (opt-in) |
| `config_path` | `""` | Custom `.stformat.json` path |
| `region` | `"all"` | `all`, `declaration`, `implementation` |
| `member` | `""` | Specific method/action/property name |
| `member_filter` | `""` | `all_methods`, `all_actions`, `all_properties` |
| `project` | `""` | `.sln` path for whole-project format |

## Typical usage

**Single file:**
```
twincat_format(path="<file.TcPOU>")
```

**Folder (recursive):**
```
twincat_format(path="<folder>")
```

**Whole project:**
```
twincat_format(project="<path-to.sln>")
```

**Declaration only:**
```
twincat_format(path="<file.TcPOU>", region="declaration")
```

**Only methods in a file:**
```
twincat_format(path="<file.TcPOU>", member_filter="all_methods")
```

**Specific method:**
```
twincat_format(path="<file.TcPOU>", member="M_Init")
```

**Dry-run (preview):**
```
twincat_format(path="<folder>", dry_run=true)
```

## What it formats

### ST Code (CDATA blocks)
- Keyword uppercasing (`if` → `IF`, `end_if` → `END_IF`)
- Tab-to-space conversion (4 spaces)
- Trailing whitespace removal
- Blank line clamping (max 1 consecutive)
- Declaration alignment (`:`, `:=`, inline comments)
- Assignment alignment (`:=` in related groups)
- FB call parameter alignment
- Boolean chain joining (short AND_THEN/OR_ELSE on one line)
- Line wrapping at configured limit
- Multiline FB call join (≤4 params back to single line)

### XML Structure
- Consistent indentation (2 spaces)
- Attribute ordering (Version, Name, Id, SpecialFunc)
- Element sorting (Declaration → Implementation → Methods/Actions/Properties alphabetically)
- CDATA formatting (empty/single-line/multi-line consistency)

### Safety
- Syntax integrity check (token count before/after)
- Atomic writes (temp file + rename)
- Backup files (`.bak`, deleted on success)
- SHA-256 change detection (skip unchanged files)
- `{formatting.disable}` / `{formatting.enable}` regions respected
- `{STweep.Disable}` / `{STweep.Enable}` markers also respected (compatibility)

## CFC / FBD files

The formatter handles CFC and FBD files safely:
- Declaration blocks (ST) are formatted
- ST Methods / Properties / Actions are formatted
- CFC/FBD Implementation XML is **never touched**

## Configuration

Defaults: `formatter/defaults.json` (matches STweep 4.5 behavior).
Project override: `.stformat.json` in project root (merged on top of defaults).

Show active config:
```
twincat_format_config(project_path="<folder>")
```

## Result interpretation

| Field | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| `success` | No hard failures |
| `total` | Files discovered |
| `formatted` | Files actually changed on disk |
| `unchanged` | Files already formatted (hash match) |
| `errors` | Files that failed (parse error, syntax integrity) |
| `dry_run` | Whether changes were only previewed |

## Do not

- Use this for STweep-specific formatting (use `twincat_stweep_format` with XAE)
- Format without checking result (`errors` field may contain syntax warnings)
- Disable `syntax_check` unless explicitly asked (prevents data corruption)
- Format files inside `{formatting.disable}` regions (the formatter skips them automatically)
